# Send every path to index.html so the app handles it.
#
# Read by Netlify AND Cloudflare Pages; ignored elsewhere, so it costs nothing
# to ship. Vercel uses vercel.json for the same thing, and a plain web server
# wants try_files (nginx) or FallbackResource (Apache) - see DEPLOY.md.
#
# Nothing in this app depends on it today: there is no router, so the only real
# path is /. But the password-reset link arrives as /?reset=<token>, and a host
# that tried to resolve an unknown path as a file would 404 before the app ever
# ran - which is a bad way to find out.
/*  /index.html  200
